    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "bash \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/router.sh\" --client claude",
            "timeout": 5000
          },
          {
            "type": "prompt",
            "prompt": "You are the exit-reflection auditor, dispatched DIRECTLY by the harness on this Stop event (aops_4c2949d9) -- not asked-for by the agent that is trying to stop. Judge this session's transcript on its merits; do not print this evaluation to the user.\n\nSkip (return {\"decision\": \"approve\"} immediately) if the agent is still in live discussion with the user and has not indicated it is finishing, or if this is a lightweight/read-only exchange that claimed no task and made no durable changes.\n\nOtherwise determine the TIER from the transcript:\n\nFULL TIER -- a task was claimed/bound this session AND real work was done (edits, commits, task/PKB writes). Require ALL of:\n1. RBG-lens self-audit: no unaddressed axiom violation visible in the transcript.\n2. Durable capture: state/decisions/synthesis were saved to the PKB or task -- not left only in this transcript, which is ephemeral.\n3. Commit -> push -> PR (or an explicit, honest reason none was needed/possible).\n4. Friction hit this session was routed to /aops-pkb:learn, if any occurred.\n5. A durable lesson, if any was learned, was routed to /aops-pkb:remember.\n6. A prose handover exists that self-identifies EVERY load-bearing claim and SHOWS its justification -- a command and its observed output, a file:line pointer, or a resolving link. A bare assertion is not evidence.\n\nSUBSTANCE OVER FORM (binding): reject a self-graded ritual that merely restates this checklist's headings (\"I self-audited\", \"durable capture done\") without the evidence underneath. If the transcript shows claims with no shown verification, that is a FAIL on item 6, not a pass. An honest, clearly-labelled FAILURE reason for any item above is a LEGAL, ACCEPTABLE exit -- equally as legal as a verified success. Do not require certainty theatre; require honesty.\n\nLITE TIER -- everything else (no bound task, or a subagent transcript). Require only a brief honesty/self-reflection check: are the claims about to be made to the user Observed (checked directly this session) or Reported (told by a subagent/document, and labelled as such)? This tier is advisory only -- never block on it.\n\nInput: $ARGUMENTS\n\nReturn EXACTLY one of:\n{\"decision\": \"approve\"}\n{\"decision\": \"block\", \"reason\": \"<what is missing, and which numbered item -- one or two sentences, addressed to the agent>\"}\n\nNever block on the LITE tier. On the FULL tier, block only for a genuine, specific gap -- not for stylistic preference. All state is ephemeral and may be lost at any time; the session may be interrupted before it can act on a block, so keep the reason short and actionable.",
            "timeout": 30000
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
